@variants

#etcsl#ms 1 ms. adds:
A.325A. [...] BI# saŋ# X [...]
?#tr.en: He was alone and, even to his sharp eyes,
?#tr.en: there was not a single person to be seen.
?#tr.en: Sleep overcame the king @noteref{i.e. @wDN{Lugalbanda}} -- sleep, the country of oppression;
?#tr.en: it is like a towering flood, like a hand demolishing a brick wall,
?#tr.en: a hand raised high, a foot raised high;
?#tr.en: covering like syrup that which is in front of it,
?#tr.en: overflowing like syrup onto that which is in front of it;
?#tr.en: it knows no overseer, knows no captain, yet it is overpowering for the hero.
?#tr.en: And by means of @wDN{Ninkasi's} wooden cask @noteref{i.e. with the help of beer}, sleep finally overcame @wDN{Lugalbanda}.
?#tr.en: He laid down @fsux{ilinnuš}, pure herb of the mountains,
?#tr.en: as a couch, he spread out a @fsux{zulumḫi} garment,
?#tr.en: he unfolded there a white linen sheet.
?#tr.en: There being no …… room for bathing,
?#tr.en: he made do with that place. The king lay down not to sleep,
?#tr.en: he lay down to dream -- not turning back at the door of the dream,
?#tr.en: not turning back at the door-pivot. To the liar it talks in lies,
?#tr.en: to the truthful it speaks truth. It can make one man happy,
?#tr.en: it can make another man sing,
?#tr.en: but it is the closed tablet-basket of the gods.
?#tr.en: It is the beautiful bedchamber of @wDN{Ninlil}, it is the counsellor of @wDN{Inana}.
?#tr.en: The multiplier of mankind,
?#tr.en: the voice of one not alive -- @wDN{Zangara},
?#tr.en: the god of dreams,
?#tr.en: himself like a bull, bellowed at @wDN{Lugalbanda}.
?#tr.en: Like the calf of a cow he lowed:
#lem: X; X; saŋ[head]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.325A

A.325B. [...]-uš im-ta-an-dub
#lem: X; dub[heap up]
#etcsl: line-id=A.325B

@endvariants
